!! FINDINGS (top)
No fail-open security fault found in the span. Three notes the lanes must know:

F1 (latent crash, fails closed, not security). `openNodeHerm` hands `p.wireVerbs` to `composeHerm` (3684-3686), and `wireVerbs` (3037) registers `sync-wiki`, `wiki-act`, `wiki-switch`, `wiki-hold`, `wiki-release`, `wiki-active` whose bodies read `wikiActivation` / `vmManager` (forward `let x!`, 1699-1700) that only `makePool` sets (3410, 3372). A herm never runs `makePool`, so those verbs throw TypeError when invoked. The wiki-verb group belongs to a wiki-bearing stack, not to the shared wiring. Any stage-cut must put them behind the wiki cap, which cures this.

F2 (silent-default hazard for T17). The pool core defaults `mountSilenceMs` to 10_000 (`HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT_MS`, vessel-island-pool-core.ts:314,395). Node overrides to 120_000/360_000 (3386-3387) because a keyhive reconverge false-timed a live mount into a fatal boot death (the comment at 3378-3385). The same 120s/3x pair also lives as `EA_SILENCE_TIMEOUT_MS`/`EA_STALL_TIMEOUT_MS` in lararium-tw5/src/daemon-vm-core.ts:134,141 (node passes no `eaSilenceMs`, 2579-2607). Three homes for one number. An injected deadline that arrives `undefined` falls to 10s and re-opens the fatal-boot bug. The default MUST be node-side.

F3 (secret crossing, by design, flag for the stage-cut). `daemonAuth` (2527-2563) carries `atom.seed` (hex), `faceAddressSecret`, `veilArchiveBytes`, `outboxKey` from main-thread custody into the daemon island. The island is the sovereign worker, not a surface, so this matches the law. It means `openDaemon`'s custody half can never be a shared stage that a surface reaches; the port that carries it must be named by capability ("holds custody for a face"), and the builder (pure) must be separated from the reads (host).

Lane collisions measured: u1's uncommitted diff (`git -C ~/.lares-scratch/u1/wt diff --stat`) touches 8 files and NOT open-node-vessel.ts or worker-handle.ts today (the lift map expected hunks at 1697/3477/3642; none stand uncommitted). ralias (`diff 27bc0cb6b`) touches open-node-vessel.ts at hunks (ralias line numbers) 1848 (residency wiring args), 1946 (systemCanon, 8 lines -> 1), 2277 (realmPlane `sealReading`), 2684 (`ring.compose` line); plus vessel-residency-wiring.ts +12 and new vessel-private.ts. Those four hunks sit inside this span.

