!! Shared facts (apply to all rows)
Contract: `VesselOrchestration<VesselIslandPool>` = {keel, wikiSlot, openDaemon, wireVerbs, afterDaemon, makePool, afterLive}, built at 3432-3438, returned in the `NodeBootPrep` record (3440-3538) next to ~25 other fields (host-shell doors, `backupDoor`, `sessionDoor`, `teardown`). `composeCoreVessel` (core-caps.ts:241) already sequences it: substrateCap(keel) -> wikiSlotCap -> daemonCap{openDaemon, wireVerbs, afterDaemon} -> wikiCap -> poolCap -> mountCap(afterLive). Order is derived from `requires`, daemon-first gate inside wiki/mount caps. `openDaemon` is ALSO exported on the prep and handed to `composeHerm` (3684) with `slot` absent (the herm decouple, `wikiBagId` etc. omitted at 2554). So `openDaemon` serves two stacks: the herm path is live code, and any cut must keep slot-optional.

Closure state the span shares with the first half (prepareNodeBootOn 709-1680), read or written here: stood[], repo, catalogHandle, storageDir, sealHome, corpusRoot, genesisDir, bootstrapPath, vesselIdentity, nexusPubkey, nexusStanding, nexusStandsAt, nexusMembership(+Holder), sovereign, custodyGroup, wornMount, activeAtom (W), wornFleetRoot (W), wornFaceProven (W), provenPlanes (RW), faceBootTiddlers (W), kahuCanon (W), kahuProtected (W), kahuStandings, kahuStandingVessel (W), shadowRing, edgeShadows, selfSlotFedGate (RW), siblingGate (W), realmPlane (RW), peerContractNymMap, charterHearthPeers, dialSeatMaps, gatePins, peerIdentifierMap, afterRoll, reverdict, representIfMoved (W), registerRelayPlanes (W), litFace (W), resweepGates (RW), landOwedHostingActs (RW), seatSettler, intentRelay, siblings (W), catalogForViews (W), storeClaim, cidDir, hermShore, sealRegistry, casBagTracker, opts, onPhase. Span-local lets (set in one closure, read in another): vmManager, wikiActivation, mailbox, daemonVm, eventBus, bootstrap, crossroadsOfferingsHandle, personaSelves, slotActiveWikiId, activeWikiSource, recallFormPalace, recallStructurePalace, recallContent, recallHolders, sourceCaptures, kelHolders, pendingVerbContribution, lightFace, nexusDial, dialStoodDown, dialAnchor. Order dependence is carried by closure assignment: `openDaemon` sets `daemonVm`/`bootstrap`-reads/`pendingVerbContribution`; `wireVerbs` THROWS if `pendingVerbContribution` is null (3240); `makePool` sets vmManager/wikiActivation/mailbox/eventBus; `afterDaemon` reads daemonVm, bootstrap, residency.
Global/clock/env/fs in the span: `process.env.LAR_SIBLING_HERMS` (2654), `console.*` throughout, `globalThis.crypto.randomUUID` (2309), `Buffer`, fs via readFileSync/existsSync (bootstrap 1898-1903), setTimeout via dialDeadlines (2341), `setCasDoor/setDyadDoor/setCustodyWriteDoor` process globals (1816, 2092, 2488: one owner per registry per process, T9's cure).
Callers of the record: composeNodeVesselOn (3596, through `composeLararium = composeCoreVessel`, node-caps.ts:142), composeNodeHermOn (3679-3686, takes three fields), plus tests (below). Workspace grep for the prep names: `prepareNodeBoot|openNodeVessel|openNodeHerm` appear in 20 files (lares-cli herm.ts, node main.ts, after-roll-chain.ts, open-daemon-vm.ts, carriage-caps.ts, browser vessel, ~9 node tests, 3 e2e).
Tests that reach the span: only through a whole boot: wire-daemon-bootstrap, kahu-canon-wiring, register-mounted-face-bags, nexus-board-climb-at-boot, open-node-vessel-composes-persona-ring, node-who-face-parity, herm-follows-realm-public, after-roll-chain, store-door-live, heavy-roster-is-complete, e2e/nexus-rekey-full-boot, e2e/persona-ring-cross-operator-admit, wire-floor-porch. No test names `wireVerbs`, `makePool`, `afterDaemon`, `afterLive`, `computeMismatch`, `signalOrExtract`, `crystallizeSignal`, `coupleSignal` (grep: only open-node-vessel.ts holds them).

