!! T12, second half: the VesselOrchestration record (1697-3538)
The row is one stage-cut, so I report per piece, then the whole.

!!! P1 residency/forward-ref block (1697-1830)
# 1697-1830. 2. Declares the forward refs, recall/capture holders (`recallFor`, `captureFor`), `sovereignRecallClient`, `realmPaceCell`, the residency wiring through `makeVesselResidency` (shared factory, tw5), and pushes ten teardown closures onto `stood`. 3. Writes closure lets listed above. 4. Callees: makeVesselResidency (tw5), makeRecallHolder/makeSourceCapture (py pipes). 5. Whole boot only. 6. Residency wiring already shared (tw5). Recall holders are host-binding (py/fs). The `stood` teardown list lifts as a typed "boot cells + teardown ledger" (T10). 7. one owner per registry (the two Map holders). 8. Risk: ralias hunk 1848 inside `makeVesselResidency` args. Verdict: NEEDS-ruling folded into T10 (cells), not a cut on its own.

!!! P2 keel (1838-2013)
# 1838-2013. 2. Builds the mesh `keel`: repo, catalogHandle, `loadGenesis` (oracle load, CAS mirror to fs, bootstrap parse + torn-face check, writes `bootstrap`), docLoadProbe/recoverCleanTail/quarantineDoc (child_process, fs), `systemCanon` (Kahu realm canon: opens the face atom, stands `kahuCanon`, protected-id holder, standings watcher), loadCorpora. 3. R/W: bootstrap, faceBootTiddlers, activeAtom, kahuCanon, kahuProtected, kahuStandingVessel, kahuStandings; fs: bootstrapPath, genesisDir, CAS dir. 4. Only `composeCoreVessel.substrateCap` (`assembleVessel(keel)`) and the herm via `p.orchestration.keel`. 5. whole boot (kahu-canon-wiring, wire-daemon-bootstrap, boot-face-planes covers `bootFacePlanes`). 6. Split:
#* bootstrap parse + torn-face check (1897-1929) -> pure reader `readBootstrapFace(tiddlers)` (the doubled-guard comment at 1889-1896 states the invariant to pin). CUT-READY, no port.
#* CAS manifest mirror (1867-1887) -> substrate adapter (fs CAS) behind "serves bytes by cid".
#* `systemCanon` (1973-2003) -> stays host/closure-bound: it opens the custody atom and writes three closure lets; ralias rewrites it. DO-NOT-CUT until ralias lands.
#* docLoadProbe/quarantine -> substrate adapter (child_process + fs); browser has its own.
## no key on a surface (loadFaceAtomOfGroup in systemCanon stays main-thread); web3-only OK. 8. Risk: ralias hunks 1946 (systemCanon) and 1848. Order: loadGenesis must write `bootstrap` before `readDaemonDoc`. 9. Red-first: a table of torn/partial bootstrap JSON (outer valid/inner truncated/non-string text/half face) -> `{}` or the named torn-face refusal; control: whole face and floor (no face) both pass. Verdict: parse+torn-face CUT-READY (C4); rest DO-NOT-CUT now.

!!! P3 wikiSlot (2016-2030)
# Reads the daemon doc's active-wiki marker, runs `selectActiveWikiSlug`, writes `activeWikiSource` and `slotActiveWikiId`, projects facets via `recipeHostFacets`. Pure but for the two closure writes and the `readDaemonDoc` read. 4. wikiSlotCap (core-caps.ts:134). Browser has its own `wikiSlot` (open-browser-vessel.ts:1152). 6. shared cap-stack stage in tw5 behind "names the active wiki slot"; the closure writes become a returned value the host reads off the slot (the composer already hands `slot` on). 8. Low risk. 9. Red: marker present/absent/arg-wins table -> {slug, source}; control: the browser twin gives the same facets for the same slug. Verdict: CUT-READY (as part of T13's slot stage, or earlier as a pure `slotFromMarker`).

!!! P4 openDaemon (2034-3030; read whole)
Ordered phases inside it (this is the "never read whole" part):
a. 2035-2082 FACE RESOLVE: sets `catalogForViews`; reads daemon doc; custody read of the founding/worn mount (`orFloor` turns `CustodyLocked` into faceless floor); face anchor; anchor-missing refusals (2062-2065); atom seed -> `activeAtom` (W); address secret (zeroed 2080); `placeAid`; atom-vs-edge key check.
b. 2089-2100 DYAD DOOR: `wornFleetRoot` (W), `shadowRing.refold`, `setDyadDoor` (process global), stood.
c. 2107-2118 dyad count log.
d. 2128-2182 PERSONA-KEL: carry up the gradient, KEL ring holder (pushed on kelHolders), fail-closed on absent chain (2151-2153), FACE PROOF (`proveFaceFromLog`, refusal throws), sets `wornFaceProved/Projection/wornFaceProven`, `provenPlanes`, raises and keeps the anchor frontier, joins face documents.
e. 2200-2209 climbs of nexus boards + crossroads pointer (unconditional, idempotent).
f. 2216-2267 REALM PLANE stand (makeRealmPlane, 25 injected ports, replaces `selfSlotFedGate`).
g. 2292-2399 FACE DIAL: `standFaceDial` (closure; sets `nexusDial`, `dialAnchor`, `representIfMoved`), the herm no-dial branch, and the LATE DIAL (`lateDialOnce`).
h. 2412-2465 CATALOG PLANE REGISTER: per-face proof (`proveOtherFace`, `proveRelayFace`), `registerRelayPlanes` (W), `provenPlanes`, `registerInCatalog` writes the catalog doc.
i. 2468-2491 custody: `litFace` (W), veil archive bytes, outbox key, `setCustodyWriteDoor` (process global).
j. 2496-2501 lease-raised anchor.
k. 2502-2526 sibling joined-face ports; `lightFace` (W).
l. 2527-2563 `daemonAuth` object (pure shape given its inputs).
m. 2568-2578 R3 plugin resolution for the daemon island; 2579-2608 `openDaemonVm` (sets `daemonVm`, `standDaemonVm()` frees the rest door).
n. 2622-2643 PersonaGroup ring: widens `selfSlotFedGate`, sets `siblingGate`.
o. 2653-2680 sibling channel (`siblings` W; reads `process.env.LAR_SIBLING_HERMS`).
p. 2690-3028 verb-provider impls (mempalaceImpl, formImpl, computeMismatch, coupleSignal, crystallizeSignal, signalOrExtract, daemonImpl, telemetryImpl) then `composeVerbPlane` -> `pendingVerbContribution`.
q. 3029 returns `{workerEa, mountMainVerbs, resolveBinding}`.
Finding: only (a) the minimum of (d)/(m) and (q) are "open the daemon VM". Phases (b), (e)-(h), (k), (n), (o) are NODE HOST SHELL work (relays, dials, gates, rings, holders) that the lift map files as R1-R19 and C6; they sit inside `openDaemon` only because the daemon needs their boards before it boots. Phase (p) is a different job again (the verb plane). So `openDaemon` fuses at least four stages: face/custody resolve (a,d,i,j,k), board stand and climb (b,e,f,n), dial and register (g,h,o), and daemon open (l,m,q) + verb providers (p).
# R/W: ~20 of the closure lets in the shared-facts list. 4. Callers: daemonCap via `o.openDaemon` (wrapper 3436) and the herm (`p.openDaemon`, 3684; slot optional). Callees: openDaemonVm (open-daemon-vm.ts -> tw5 openDaemonVmCore), makeRealmPlane, standSiblingChannel, composeVerbPlane (tw5 verb-caps), many custody reads. 5. Whole boot only (nexus-rekey-full-boot e2e, persona-ring e2e, nexus-board-climb-at-boot, register-mounted-face-bags). 6. Lift target: NO single target. Per phase: (l) pure `buildDaemonAuth(inputs)` CUT-READY; (a) split into custody reads (substrate adapter: "holds custody for a face") and a pure decision `resolveBootFace` (floor vs lit vs refuse; the three throws at 2062-2065, 2073, 2082) CUT-READY as a decision table; (d) face proof is already pure (`proveFaceFromLog`) with host reads; stays host, ports "reads the face log"; (e)-(h)(n)(o) -> T13 shared stages one PR each; (m) host binding (worker_threads daemon island); (p) see T14. 7. Laws: no key on a surface (F3, atom seed/outbox key stay main-thread, only the island receives them); one owner per registry (b, i set process-global doors; also `setDyadDoor(null)` on teardown clobbers a second vessel in-process); no global now (OK: fold waits are causal, "never on a clock", 2086-2088); web3-only OK. Fail-closed seams to PRESERVE in any cut: absent KEL chain halts (2151), face proof refusal throws (2165), anchor-missing throws (2062-2065), `deviceAside` returns true when no shadows ring (2638), dyad door answers `aside` on a failed fold (2096), sibling channel refuses alone and never the vessel (2661-2663). A cut that turns a throw into a returned `{ok:false}` must keep the boot refusing. 8. Risk: highest of the batch. Hidden order: `siblingGate` (n) must be set before (o) reads it; `selfSlotFedGate` is replaced in (f) then composed in (n), so f before n; `standDaemonVm()` (2608) unblocks the rest door that awaits the island's leg; `pendingVerbContribution` set at the very end gates `wireVerbs`. Failure-mode flips: a torn-vs-floor misread flips closed (refuse) to open (faceless boot); moving any of d/f/n after the daemon open would let the island's first ask read a stale fold (2086-2088 comment). ralias hunks 2277 and 2684 land inside f and n. 9. Red-first: per extracted decision, a table with the refusal rows asserted by name, control = floor and whole face; for the stage-cut as a whole, T6 boot characterization pins phase order via a recorded-trace mutant (swap f and n) that must go red. Verdict: DO-NOT-CUT as one piece. NEEDS-RULING on the fork: split `openDaemon` into named stages (face-resolve, boards, dial, daemon-open, verb-plane) each behind a capability port, or keep it one closure and extract only pure deciders. Lean: pure deciders first (resolveBootFace, buildDaemonAuth, bootstrap reader), stage-split inside T12 only after T6 pins the order.

!!! P5 wireVerbs (3037-3244)
# Registers on the main verb table: seedVesselDefaults, sync-wiki, wiki-act (slot routing 3049-3070), residency, the store door table (`storeDoorReactors`), realm-bag, realm-bags, nexus-rekey, nexus-reshare, cas-sweep tick (`installCasSweep`, pushes a teardown), cas-fetch, cad-seal, wiki-switch/hold/release/active, then applies `pendingVerbContribution` (throws if null). 3. R: wikiActivation, vmManager, slotActiveWikiId, daemonVm, realmPlane, activeAtom, sealRegistry, cidDir, genesisDir, storeClaim.bootEpoch. W: `stood`. 4. daemonCap via `deps.wireVerbs` (core-caps.ts:122) after openDaemon awaited, before `mountMainVerbs`; herm too (F1). 5. whole boot (store-door-live, nexus-rekey-full-boot). 6. Split by capability: wiki group (sync-wiki, wiki-act routing, wiki-switch/hold/release/active) -> shared tw5 stage behind "activates wikis by reference" + a pool port (browser hand-repeats wiki-switch at open-browser-vessel.ts:1521+); wiki-act's `slot()` regex + target choice (3053-3062) is a pure router: CUT-READY. Cas group (cas-sweep, cas-fetch, nexus-reshare) -> host fs. Custody/charter group (nexus-rekey, cad-seal, realm-bag(s), store doors) stay host: they use custody doors and quorum signers (no key on a surface). 7. one owner per registry: the main verb table is the registry; verbs register once. 8. Risk: F1; `installCasSweep` registers a timer (stood). Withholds sweep when genesis protect set unreadable (3143): fails closed, preserve. 9. Red: for the router, a table (verb x from/to bag x `wiki` arg -> target) with the daemon-slot exclusion row; control: the active-slot fallback. For F1: compose a herm and assert the wiki verbs are absent (red today, they register and crash). Verdict: wiki-act router CUT-READY; wiki group NEEDS-RULING (lean: lift to the wiki cap in T13 so the herm drops it); host groups DO-NOT-CUT.

!!! P6 afterDaemon (3247-3297)
# Pins boot bags in residency, replays durable pins, starts the sweeper, attaches residency to the composite, stands the sync gates once (`resweepGates`), lands owed hosting acts, kicks `seatSettler`. 3. R: bootstrap, daemonVm; RW: resweepGates, landOwedHostingActs. Fire-and-forget `void ... .catch(warn)` at 3273, 3291, 3264. 4. daemonCap (shared) and the herm. 6. Pin list (3248-3260) -> pure `bootPins(assembly, bootstrap)` CUT-READY (lift map's "boot pin list"); sweeper/pins are the shared residency cap; sync gates and hosting land are host shell (gate custody). 7. no global now: pins and sweeper are event-fed; fine. 8. RISK flagged: `standSyncGates` failure only warns (3273). If the gates do not stand, what the Repo's share policy defaults to is decided in the first half (1514+, outside my span); I did not read it, so I cannot say whether a failed gate stand leaves peers denied or open. NEEDS the first-half reader to confirm fail-closed before anyone moves this. 9. Red: bootPins table (with/without lares handle, with/without face); control: same list the pre-cut code pinned. Verdict: pin list CUT-READY; rest DO-NOT-CUT until the gate-stand fail-mode is confirmed.

!!! P7 makePool (3310-3418) and T17 constants
# Builds the mailbox, event bus and its rings, subscribes worker events to the daemon, builds `diskMirrorGrant` from `kahuCanon` and `nexusStanding.kind`, constructs `VesselIslandPool` (mainRepo, portPolicy, storage, mount deadlines, plugin resolver, grants, event hooks), wires it through `residencyWiring.wireToPool`, returns the pool. 3. R: kahuCanon, nexusStanding, corpusRoot, crossroadsOfferingsHandle, opts.portPolicy/onPortMessage, wornGateFace; W: mailbox, eventBus, vmManager, wikiActivation. 4. poolCap (core-caps.ts:175). 5. whole boot; the pool itself has tests (vessel-island-pool, pool-mount-intensity, mesh pool-*), not this assembly. 6. `diskMirrorGrant` (3332-3366) -> pure `diskMirrorGrantFor({kahuCanon, root, guardNexusHandles})` CUT-READY; the pool construction is a substrate adapter (worker_threads) behind "spawns wiki islands", already `VesselIslandPoolCore` + host; mailbox/eventBus keel mechanisms. 7. The default `portPolicy` is closed: `edits:false, bags:[], admin:false` (3375). Preserve. 8. Risk: ralias touches `kahuCanon` upstream; order: `diskMirrorGrant` reads `kahuCanon` at pool-build time (after systemCanon ran in substrate). 9. Red: grant table (lares/lararium present or absent -> grants omitted entirely; charter vs non-charter -> guardNexusHandles); control: crossroads/working/self rows always present. Verdict: diskMirrorGrant CUT-READY; pool construction DO-NOT-CUT (substrate adapter, leave).

!!! P8 afterLive (3421-3430)
One line: pin the home wiki as a `wiki` grain in residency. Shared cap hook (browser has `afterLive` at 1864). Verdict: CUT-READY into the shared mount stage with the residency port; trivial.

!!! P9 backup door and the return record (3440-3538)
`backupDoor` (3466-3527): `ownEdgeShadowed` (3468-3475, fold-3-times-then-standing, fails CLOSED to "shadowed" on fold failure: preserve), and three getters `cutMemory`, `memoryDoor`, `importMemory` each repeating the same `askIslandMemory({daemonHandle, placeVerb, act, ..., vesselKey, sign})` block with an identical 4-line sign closure (3485-3488, 3504-3507, 3519-3522) plus `dropFace` and the `askIslandVerb` closure at 3086-3089. Pure duplicate: one `askMemory(act, facts)` helper deletes 25 lines. The `sign` closure signs with `activeAtom` on the host: the key stays in these closures, and the answer carries only section/door/results (no key crosses). 4. Consumers: composeNodeVesselOn/HermOn return `p.backupDoor`; lares-cli reads the door. 5. tests: custody backup tests reach it elsewhere (not read). Verdict: CUT-READY (dedupe), no port.

!!! T12 whole: verdict
NEEDS-RULING, not a single cut. The lift map is right that the seam exists (composeCoreVessel) but it understates the width: `openDaemon` carries four jobs and half of `wireVerbs` is host custody. Fork for the operator: (A) T12 splits the record into stages along the five-job line above, or (B) T12 only extracts pure deciders and moves the wiki group; stage-split waits for T13. Lean B first (deciders + wiki verb group + dedupe + diskMirrorGrant + bootPins), because it cures F1, takes no ordering risk, and leaves T6's pins to guard the later split. The record returned at 3440-3538 should split into `{orchestration}` and `{hostShell}` the way the lift map says; the composer needs only `orchestration`, the herm needs `keel/openDaemon/wireVerbs/afterDaemon`.

